WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 size:88% position:44%
-I want to talk, though,
about your beginnings.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
You first started acting,
you were in L.A...

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...going to school

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be an actor.
-Born and raised, yeah.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.210 size:78% position:39%
-And Central Casting,
and they put this up

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.046 size:84% position:42%
on Instagram recently,
that three of the stars

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the show, there you are
in today's day.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
There you are, that that's me.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's you.
-That's me, yeah.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
I look very different
on the show.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:22.489 size:78% position:39%
-I have to say, like,
you do things that

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would not have predicted.
-Chameleon!

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, these are
your original head shots,

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:29.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
the three of you.
So, what was Central Casting?

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Central Casting is
background-actors' casting,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.368 line:92%
so when you watch anything

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.303
and it looks like people
are just living their life

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:40.740 size:78% position:39%
and there's strangers
walking around them,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.411
those are all paid actors
who are just "extras"...

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...in the background,

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
and for one summer
during college,

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did that as,
like, my summer job.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had never been
on a set before.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:56.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was going to theater school,
and the RA from my building

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
graduated and was working
for Central Casting.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he was like,
"Oh, come do this.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:04.764 size:84% position:42%
And I'll get you all
the 'good' extra jobs."

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.300 line:92%
-So, what's a "good" extra job?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.401 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Well, I had a couple.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:12.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was definitely, like,
on that show "American Dreams"

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
and would be, like,
one of five girls

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
smoking a cigarette
in the bathroom

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
while, like,
a scene was happening.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:22.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, most notably,
I got to play a dead body...

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, that's great.
-...on "NYPD Blue"...

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.119 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-That's really great.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...in the
Mark-Paul Gosselaar years.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.458
I'm not sure how long --
was he always on that show?

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he was on,
like, at the tail-end.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
the last couple years, yeah.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When he was on,
which was major for me

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I am a huge
"Saved by the Bell" fan

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
and grew up watching
that so much.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was just like,
"Oh, my God.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
What am I gonna do
when I see him?"

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Every time you watched
"Saved by the Bell"

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.407
you were like, "Oh, my God.
I would be so psyched to be dead

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of Zack."
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My dream is to be,
like, lying, holding my breath

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:57.250
in front of Zack Morris,
and have him pull a receipt

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.419
out of my pocket,
which was the action that he did

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the show.
It was, like, a major clue

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the episode.
-So, you have to be

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:06.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
a dead person...
-I'm dead, like, in a closet.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-And he finds me

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
with another cop,
and they, like,

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.466
squat and have a serious scene,
and then they find a receipt

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, pull it
out of my pocket.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:16.436 line:92%
I was so excited about it.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.271 line:92%
When it aired, it was just legs.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.907 size:75% position:38%
It was just my legs.
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that receipt, you know,
and it's the worst

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause being a dead body
is actually quite challenging.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've played a few.
-Oh, I'm sure it was harder

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
than what
Mark Gosselaar was doing.

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
He's like, "Ba-ba-ba-ba-ba."

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-I'm having to, like,

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.990
really be --
"inhabit the corpse" mind-set...

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...and feel dead,

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:42.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
and hold your breath,
like, 'cause they're like,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.163 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Background girl, stop.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.698
We can see you breathing.
You're not holding your breath."

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah!
And then, they've got to rifle

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.502 size:78% position:39%
through your pockets!
That can't be easy.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and they're,
like, touching your body

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're, like,
pretending not to be excited.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.577
-It's like dead bodies just,
like, don't react to, like,

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.646
their high school crushes.
-The director was, like,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.381 line:92%
a real Nazi about not reacting.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:04.918
-I was like, "She's dead,
but she's not that dead."

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience laughs ]

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:10.356
-And then, so that is obviously
incredibly important work.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, it was good.
-But you also did some --

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were a clown.
You did some clowning.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:17.597 size:75% position:38%
-Yes, prior to this.
In preparation for.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.265 line:92%
-So, clown was before this.

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:23.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
It goes clown, dead body,
where you are now.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:26.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and then now!
That's just like every actor's

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:26.973 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
normal trajectory.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:30.410
So, when I was in high school,
maybe right after high school --

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause again, these are,
like, my summer jobs.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:35.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Um, I worked as a clown.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:38.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some of my friends
from Drama class

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
became clowns.
I'm going to do the rest

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the story like this.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.091 line:92%
-I have a weird tic these days.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:51.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, so, it was
a bounce house company.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.733 size:75% position:38%
who was just getting
into the clown game.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-So they...

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you're already
on the lost, so to speak.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
If people are going to pay
for a bounce house,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.306
they might throw in money.
-Maybe they also want that.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:05.144
So, it was out of
this huge warehouse in Compton,

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:07.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Straight Outta Compton."
[ Audience laughs ]

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.983
-Well, that does establish
you don't -- I will say I saw

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Straight Outta Compton"
the film, and I don't remember

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
a single clown.
-It got cut for time.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it got cut for time.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw a dead clown's legs,
but was that you?

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:22.295 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience laughs ]

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:23.363 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-And it was comical.

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:25.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I grew up
in Los Angeles

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
in South Pasadena,
which is not quite

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
the same thing,
and before every party,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had to go to
the warehouse in Compton,

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:37.010
pick up your clown outfit,
like, do your clown makeup,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then go to
the nearest gas station

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:42.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they paid us
for gas mileage,

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:45.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they were, like,
measuring from the place.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.919 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And so, just picture me.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm 17 years old.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.757 line:92%
I have, like, a yellow fro.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:51.624 size:84% position:42% line:92%
My clown name is Sunny.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:55.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm just, like,
pumping gas in Compton

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.930 size:84% position:42% line:92%
like it ain't no thing.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.832 line:92%
And definitely, it was not.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:00.466 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Nobody cared.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, my God.
What's gonna happen?"

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.371 size:78% position:39%
And people were like,
"What's up, clown?"

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience laughs ]

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was like, "Cool."

